# Explain What You Built

## After every completed feature or fix, provide a plain-English summary:

1. **What was built** — one sentence describing the feature or fix
2. **Files created or changed** — list each file and what it does in one line
3. **How it connects** — how the new code fits into the existing system
4. **What to test** — the specific user action to verify it works

## Example:

> **Built:** Generate social post endpoint
>
> **Files:**
> - `app/api/ai/generate/route.ts` — API route that takes a brief and returns generated content
> - `lib/ai/prompts.ts` — added `generateSocialPost` prompt template
> - `lib/ai/generate.ts` — added `callAnthropic` function
>
> **Connects to:** Called by the Generate button on the project page. Uses brand context from the database.
>
> **Test:** Go to a project, type a brief, click Generate, verify output appears.

## Why this matters
The project owner does not read code. This summary is the only way they understand what changed. Without it, the codebase becomes a black box.
